-- help-account-add.txt --
Create or repair an account (settings, shared files, push guard, usage, login)

Usage:
  srn account add [<provider>/]<name> [flags]

Examples:
  srn account add work                     asks for the profile, usage tracking and login
  srn account add claude/work --profile strict --usage --login
  srn account add work --with privacy      also turn telemetry off
  srn account add work --relink            link files the account has its own copy of (keeps a backup)

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for add
      --login            log in right away without asking
      --no-login         do not log in and do not ask
      --no-usage         do not track usage limits and do not ask
      --profile string   settings profile for a new account: minimal, standard, strict (default standard)
      --relink           move the account's own copies of shared files aside (.bak-<time>) and link them to main (asks)
      --usage            track usage limits in the status line without asking
      --with strings     opt-in settings, repeatable: privacy, no-attribution
  -y, --yes              do not ask; use the defaults and the flags given

Global Flags:
  -a, --account string   account to run as (provider/name or name)
  -C, --dir string       run as if started in this directory
      --no-color         disable colors (also: NO_COLOR=1)
