-- help-grid.txt --
Run agents side by side in a tmux grid for <repo>: one pane per agent, each in its own
worktree. Running grid again for the same repository adds panes.

Usage:
  srn grid <repo> [<account>:]<name>... [flags]
  srn grid [command]

Examples:
  srn grid ~/repo feat-a personal:fix-b          per-agent account (default: main or -a)
  srn grid ~/repo feat-a claude/personal:fix-b   account as provider/name
  srn grid ~/repo feat-1 feat-2 --spread         round-robin over logged-in accounts
  srn grid ls | attach [repo] | stop [repo]

Available Commands:
  attach      Attach to the grid of a repository (default: this one)
  ls          List running grids
  stop        Stop the grid of a repository and every agent in it (worktrees are kept)

Flags:
  -h, --help     help for grid
      --spread   spread unprefixed names over logged-in accounts

Global Flags:
  -a, --account string   account to run as (provider/name or name)
  -C, --dir string       run as if started in this directory
      --no-color         disable colors (also: NO_COLOR=1)

