-- help-swap.txt --
Move a conversation to another account and resume it there, e.g. when an account hits its
usage limit. Without arguments the conversation is the one that last hit its limit in this
directory (or below it), or one running here; several candidates are offered in a picker. The
target account is --to, else picked from the accounts ranked by their usage.

A running session is stopped first (asks; in a grid its pane is restarted in place). Moving a
conversation to an account of another organization asks first too. When the target account
already holds the conversation and it went on there, the swap is refused unless --force.

--worktree <name> moves the latest conversation of that agent worktree instead.

Usage:
  srn swap [flags]

Examples:
  srn swap                              the conversation that just hit its limit here
  srn swap --to personal                the same, to claude/personal
  srn swap --worktree feat-a --to work  latest conversation of worktree feat-a
  srn swap --session <id> --to work     any conversation, by session ID

Flags:
  -f, --force             move it even if the target's copy went on and differs
  -h, --help              help for swap
      --session string    session ID of the conversation to move
      --to string         account to move it to
      --worktree string   move the latest conversation of this agent worktree
  -y, --yes               do not ask for confirmation

Global Flags:
  -a, --account string   account to run as (provider/name or name)
  -C, --dir string       run as if started in this directory
      --no-color         disable colors (also: NO_COLOR=1)
