-- help-self-update.txt --
Update squadrn and its plugin in every account to the newest release of your channel.
--check only looks and shows the release notes; --rollback goes back to the release installed
before.

Usage:
  srn self-update [flags]

Examples:
  srn self-update --check       what is new
  srn self-update               install the newest release of your channel
  srn self-update --rollback    go back to the release installed before

Flags:
      --allow-downgrade   install a release older than the running one
      --check             only report whether an update is available, with its release notes
  -h, --help              help for self-update
      --json              with --check: print JSON (current, latest, channel, available, notes)
      --repo string       GitHub repository to update from (owner/name)
      --rollback          reinstall the release that was installed before this one
      --tag string        install this release (v1.2.3) instead of the newest

Global Flags:
  -a, --account string   account to run as (provider/name or name)
  -C, --dir string       run as if started in this directory
      --no-color         disable colors (also: NO_COLOR=1)
