-- help-account-adopt.txt --
Make an existing config dir an account, then set it up like account add. Its own settings are
kept: they become the account's copy, and keys that differ from main's stay as they are.

Usage:
  srn account adopt [<provider>/]<name> [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for adopt
      --profile string   settings profile to apply (default: none, keep its settings)
  -y, --yes              do not ask; use the defaults

Global Flags:
  -a, --account string   account to run as (provider/name or name)
  -C, --dir string       run as if started in this directory
      --no-color         disable colors (also: NO_COLOR=1)
-- help-usage-setup.txt --
Record an account's usage through its status line: the status line command in the account's
settings.json is wrapped, so squadrn sees what Claude Code reports while your own command keeps
running and showing. Each account has its own settings.json, so each is set up on its own.

Usage:
  srn usage setup [<account>] [flags]

Flags:
      --all    every account
  -h, --help   help for setup
      --undo   restore the previous status line
  -y, --yes    do not ask for confirmation

Global Flags:
  -a, --account string   account to run as (provider/name or name)
  -C, --dir string       run as if started in this directory
      --no-color         disable colors (also: NO_COLOR=1)
